  <h2>Notice and repair the reporting relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="an" data-hint="News is uncountable, so one item needs a countable product or unit noun." data-fix="I read an interesting news report this morning. / I read an interesting piece of news this morning." data-why="News is uncountable and cannot follow an by itself; news report and piece of news create countable units." data-success-message="Correct. The repair adds a countable unit instead of treating news as a count noun.">
    <h3>Repair 1: use uncountable <span class="ex">news</span></h3><p>Tap the article that cannot stand directly before uncountable <span class="ex">news</span>.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I read</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="an">an</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="interesting">interesting news</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="morning">this morning.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="says" data-hint="According to already introduces the source noun." data-fix="According to the report, costs fell in May. / The report says costs fell in May." data-why="According to plus a source noun and source plus says are two separate attribution frames." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence now uses one complete attribution frame.">
    <h3>Repair 2: choose one attribution frame</h3><p>Tap the verb that duplicates the source structure.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="according">According to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="report">the report</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="says">says</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="costs">costs fell in May.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="proves" data-hint="The evidence is one unidentified post with no confirmation." data-fix="One unidentified post claims the airport is closed, but the closure remains unverified." data-why="One unidentified and unconfirmed post is not enough evidence to present the closure as proved." data-success-message="Correct. Claims reports the post’s statement, and unverified preserves the current evidence status.">
    <h3>Repair 3: reduce unsupported certainty</h3><p>Tap the verb that makes the evidence sound conclusive.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="one">One unidentified post</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="proves">proves</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="airport">the airport</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="closed">is closed.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice verification without revealing a real feed or belief</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to reveal a real political belief, voting history, browsing history, search history, private message, social-media account, workplace, source contact, location, health event, legal problem, traumatic event, family conflict, or story you regret sharing. Use Metrovale, Clearwater, and tutor-supplied fictional material. A real current story is optional and should be used only when the learner wants to discuss it.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Chain map:</b> Name the publisher, author, source, claim, evidence, missing context, and current verification status.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Headline repair:</b> Preserve the strongest supported result while restoring its category, place, timeframe, and uncertainty.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Independence check:</b> Decide whether several reports used separate evidence or copied one press release, wire item, quotation, or dataset.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Correction route:</b> If you repeated an inaccurate claim, state what was wrong, provide the corrected scope, cite the evidence, and avoid hiding the correction.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second fictional verification-desk briefing</h3>
    <p>Use the Clearwater file. Identify the viral item’s format and central claim; name the memo’s publisher and evidence; explain exactly what fell by 80% and what fell by 9%; show why the citywide framing is misleading; distinguish the city memo from the independent researcher’s comment; rewrite the headline with accurate scope; give a two-sentence attributed summary; recommend one next check; and answer one editor question. Use at least six target chunks and make <span class="ex">news, headline, report, reliable, source</span>, and the noun-verb stress contrast in <span class="ex">record</span> intelligible.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener recover the product type, publisher, author if supplied, source, exact claim, evidence, category, denominator or baseline, timeframe, context, uncertainty, independent confirmation, and responsible next action without the speaker adding unsupported certainty?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved uncountable news, distinguished a press release from independent confirmation, separated a supported fact from a checkable claim, calibrated an inference, interpreted a percentage with scope, and selected a responsible correction.">
    <h3>Final check: choose the media account the evidence can defend</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I read a news report and then checked two pieces of evidence." data-hint="News is uncountable; report and pieces create countable units." data-fix="I read a news report and then checked two pieces of evidence."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence uses <span class="ex">news</span> and <span class="ex">evidence</span> naturally?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I read a news report and then checked two pieces of evidence.">I read a news report and then checked two pieces of evidence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I read a news and then checked two evidences.">I read a news and then checked two evidences.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I newsed two evidence reports.">I newsed two evidence reports.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The company release is primary evidence for what the company announced, but separate reporting is needed for independent confirmation." data-hint="Primary source and independent confirmation answer different questions." data-fix="The company release is primary evidence for what the company announced, but separate reporting is needed for independent confirmation."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence accurately describes a company press release?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The company release is primary evidence for what the company announced, but separate reporting is needed for independent confirmation.">The company release is primary evidence for what the company announced, but separate reporting is needed for independent confirmation.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every press release is automatically false because an organization produced it.">Every press release is automatically false because an organization produced it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A press release automatically confirms every company claim independently.">A press release automatically confirms every company claim independently.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A factual claim can be checked; the record supports presenting this particular date as a fact." data-hint="Checkability describes the claim type; adequate evidence supports fact status here." data-fix="A factual claim can be checked; the record supports presenting this particular date as a fact."><p class="quiz-question">3. The certified record establishes the meeting date. Which statement preserves the difference between a factual claim and a supported fact?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A factual claim can be checked; the record supports presenting this particular date as a fact.">A factual claim can be checked; the record supports presenting this particular date as a fact.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every checkable sentence is automatically true before anyone checks it.">Every checkable sentence is automatically true before anyone checks it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A fact is only a personal preference that cannot use evidence.">A fact is only a personal preference that cannot use evidence.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The early pattern may suggest stronger demand, but the sample is too small for a firm conclusion." data-hint="Keep the small sample and use may suggest for a cautious inference." data-fix="The early pattern may suggest stronger demand, but the sample is too small for a firm conclusion."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which summary matches a small preliminary sample?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The early pattern may suggest stronger demand, but the sample is too small for a firm conclusion.">The early pattern may suggest stronger demand, but the sample is too small for a firm conclusion.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The small sample proves permanent demand in every market.">The small sample proves permanent demand in every market.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The sample is small, so every recorded number is automatically false.">The sample is small, so every recorded number is automatically false.</button></div></div>
