  <h2>Reflect: what role does each piece of information play?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">A headline is not proof because...</span> <span class="ex">A primary source can tell us...</span> <span class="ex">Independent confirmation requires...</span> <span class="ex">A factual claim differs from a supported fact because...</span> <span class="ex">Unverified does not mean...</span> <span class="ex">Bias does not automatically mean...</span> <span class="ex">According to differs from says because...</span> <span class="ex">A percentage needs...</span></p>
    <p>Take one dramatic fictional headline and rebuild its chain: format, publisher, author, source, exact claim, evidence, context, current status, uncertainty, independent check, corrected headline, and responsible summary. Remove no real supported result, but add no certainty that the evidence cannot carry.</p>
